                        <p>One of the most highlighting elements of an individual’s beauty, be it male or female, is hair. However, hair loss is a common problem these day. Follicular Unit Extraction or FUE is one of the most prominent techniques to overcome baldness and hair loss. You might be wondering what the FUE hair transplant technique is. This is a technique discovered in the late ’90s to enable hair growth by utilizing a person’s own follicular units. Before undergoing the procedure, it is important to understand the FUE hair transplant pros and cons.</p>

                        <h3 class="blog_heading">What guidelines should I follow before undergoing an FUE procedure?</h3>
                        <p>An individual must get a consultation to understand if he/she is the right candidate for FUE hair transplant treatment. Once that is done, the following guidelines can help you prepare:</p>
                        <ol style="margin-left: 40px;">
                            <li>It is important to inform the doctor about any blood thinners or otherwise strong medication you are taking.</li>
                            <li>As per the advice, it is necessary to stop consuming vitamin B/E or any anti-inflammatory medication, one week before the treatment</li>
                            <li>It is crucial to skip a head wash, use any hair products, and dyes on the day of the treatment as per the doctor’s orders.</li>
                            <li>Any necessary medication of heart and blood pressure should be continued even on the day of the procedure and any prescribed inhalers must be carried along.</li>
                            <li>You must skip out on smoking and drinking at least two weeks before the procedure as it may hinder the healing process</li>
                        </ol>
                        <p>For any of these guidelines, it is important to consult with the best FUE hair transplant doctors.</p>

                        <h3 class="blog_heading">How does FUE Hair Transplant work?</h3>
                        <p>Over time, the follicles live through the three-way cycle of growth and regrowth. Gradually, the strength of these follicles declines and the hair growth eventually comes to a halt in those particular areas. Through the FUE hair transplant procedure, the weak follicles are replaced with those that still have the strength to grow hair. This way, after the FUE hair transplant surgery and the completion of the natural healing process, hair growth starts again.</p>
                        
                        <h3 class="blog_heading">Targeted Areas for Treatment</h3>
                        <p>FUE hair transplant treatment is specific to hair growth. The most commonly targeted area is the scalp. Some might even be interested in having hair growth on arms, legs, and even the genital area. The treatment depends on the choice of the targeted area for every individual.</p>
                        
                        <h3 class="blog_heading">How long does it Take?</h3>
                        <p>At one time only a certain targeted area is treated upon. A single sitting might take about four hours or more as it is a delicate procedure. After every session, it might take about 10 days to get the stitches removed and additional few days for the natural healing to take place. Several sessions are set months apart to enable complete healing of the previously treated area.</p>
                        
                        <h3 class="blog_heading">Are you a good candidate for FUE Hair Transplant?</h3>
                        <p>Before opting for the FUE hair transplant procedure, it is necessary to confirm that it is indeed the right choice for you. Is the FUE hair transplant good or bad for you? You can cross out the points from the checklist below.</p>
                        <ol style="margin-left: 40px;">
                            <li>There is a certain level of baldness up to which this procedure is beneficial. It is necessary to consult with your doctor to know if you lie in the right range to get the procedure started.</li>
                            <li>Men who wish for short haircuts are eligible for the FUE hair transplant treatment.</li>
                            <li>Individuals who have previously undergone the treatment, and need a correction can opt for this.</li>
                            <li>If you require the hair transplant to go from your body to your scalp, then you can opt for it as well.</li>
                            <li>If you are suffering from tightness in the scalp after undergoing FUT, you can also go for the corrective FUE procedure.</li>
                        </ol>
                        <p>If you lie anywhere in the above categories, you are a good candidate for an FUE hair transplant.</p>

                        <h3 class="blog_heading">How long do the results last for FUE Hair Transplant?</h3>
                        <p>Theoretically, the effects must last a lifetime after FUE hair transplant surgery. However, this might not always be the case as the follicles are programmed genetically for hair growth. It also depends on their age, type of hair, initial extent of hair fall experienced, the strength of the follicles, etc. Some individuals might require multiple procedures to retain the desired results of the treatment.</p>

                        <h3 class="blog_heading">Side effects of FUE Procedure</h3>
                        <p>It is assumed that there would not be any visible scars from the procedure except for some tiny white dots that would fade with time. These white dots are the points of follicle extraction and replacement. But you might experience other side effects like:</p>
                        <ol style="margin-left: 40px;">
                            <li>Infection</li>
                            <li>Crust formation</li>
                            <li>Pain after FUE hair transplant or even swelling of the surgery site</li>
                            <li>Follicle swelling</li>
                            <li>Bleeding</li>
                            <li>Numbness</li>
                            <li>The different look of the transplanted hair as compared to surrounding hair</li>
                            <li>Balding and hair loss persists</li>
                        </ol>
                        <p>In the case of any of these side effects experienced, you must inform the doctor immediately.</p>

                        <h3 class="blog_heading">Is FUE Hair Transplant a successful procedure?</h3>
                        <p>There have been cases where people have opted for over-the-counter hair restoration products over surgeries and have faced disappointment. That is because the FUE hair transplant procedure has been seen to lead towards a better and successful treatment outcome. However, it depends on the pre-conditions of the hair follicles, the success as wel as accuracy rate of the procedure performed. Therefore, it is important to get a thorough consultation before understanding your condition and guarantee a higher success rate.</p>

                        <h3 class="blog_heading">FUE Hair Transplant recovery process</h3>
                        <p>You might question ‘is FUE hair transplant safe’ and what happens afterward. Some people are often concerned, and the question ‘is FUE hair transplant painful’ in the long run. It is not. The overall recovery process of the treatment is quick and, to an extent, painless as well. One might experience some swelling and discomfort for about three days after the procedure. But the recovery completely depends on the accuracy of the procedure and the aftercare.</p>

                        <h3 class="blog_heading">Post-treatment guidelines after the FUE procedure</h3>
                        <p>Post-FUE hair transplant care is absolutely imperative to ensure a speedy recovery. Well, you can follow with this aftercare to make sure all is well.</p>
                        <ol style="margin-left: 40px;">
                            <li>Avoid washing hair for at least three days, and be careful while washing afterward.</li>
                            <li>Use gentle and light shampoos for about a couple of weeks after the surgery, as harsh products might be harmful to the healing skin.</li>
                            <li>It is better to take a few days off work and take rest to avoid any unnecessary strenuous activity that might hinder the healing process.</li>
                            <li>You must avoid using hair brushes for at least a couple of weeks to promote the healing process.</li>
                            <li>Ask the doctor for advice before wearing any hair accessories like hats, beanies, or any other covering cloth.</li>
                        </ol>
                        <p>You might notice hair fall at the beginning of the healing process. This is quite normal. You may start noticing the actual growth and positive difference after 3-4 months.</p>

                        <h3 class="blog_heading">Conclusion</h3>
                        <p>The FUE hair transplant process is a tricky one. It’s accuracy and success depend solely on the expertise of the surgeon. The average cost of FUE hair transplant in India is between Rs.3 lakhs to Rs.12.2 lakhs. The FUE hair transplant cost also depends on the number of hair follicles being transplanted, and the amount of the scalp area being treated. India has some of the best doctors, who are highly experienced with the FUE hair transplant procedure and, can provide the best before, during, and aftercare at the best prices.</p>
                        <p>In some cases, people might undergo FUE hair transplant treatment but see no visible effects and no positive outcome. Such people can opt for a more professional doctor who has done a noticeable number of successful cases. Consultation with such a doctor can put their minds at ease and help them decide on a repeat treatment, this time with a higher success rate.</p>
